# ── apps/ml/.gitignore ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Datasets and trained models are NOT committed to git.
#   (1) size:    git keeps every version forever → bloated clones for everyone.
#   (2) license: some sets (e.g. the Technical Debt Dataset, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
#                restrict redistribution.
# Keep only the folder structure (.gitkeep) + data/README.md; download locally.
# A tiny SAMPLE for automated tests may be committed — add an explicit `!` rule.

# all dataset contents (raw / interim / processed / external + any loose files)
data/**
!data/**/
!data/README.md

# trained model artifacts
models/**
!models/**/
*.pkl
*.joblib

# keep folder placeholders everywhere
!**/.gitkeep

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.env
